      en: "The Hollywood Bowl is a premier outdoor amphitheater situated deep within the Hollywood Hills of Los Angeles, California. Opened in 1922, the venue is instantly recognized by its iconic, visually striking banded acoustic shell, originally designed with input from prominent architects including Frank Lloyd Wright Jr. Serving as the prestigious summer home of the Los Angeles Philharmonic, the natural acoustic bowl accommodates over 17,000 spectators for spectacular evening performances under the stars. Throughout its century-long history, the stage has hosted legendary musical acts ranging from The Beatles and Frank Sinatra to legendary classical composers and massive cinematic film score events. Music K6 â€” iconic musical venues."
